{"name":"Marshmallow Fluff","hex":"#faf3de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marshmallow fluff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Marshmallow creme."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marshmallow_fluff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marshmallow creme","blocks":[{"text":"Marshmallow creme is a marshmallow confectionery spread similar in flavor, but not texture, to regular solid marshmallow. One brand of marshmallow creme is Marshmallow Fluff, which is used to make the fluffernutter sandwich, a New England classic comfort food which debuted in 1918 in Massachusetts, just a year after marshmallow creme was invented."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Marshmallow_fluff2.jpg/330px-Marshmallow_fluff2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshmallow_creme","wikidata":"Q2915519"},{"title":"Marshmallow","blocks":[{"text":"Marshmallow is a confection made from sugar, water and gelatin whipped to a solid-but-soft consistency. It is used as a filling in baking or molded into shapes and coated with corn starch. This sugar confection is inspired by a medicinal confection made from Althaea officinalis, the marsh-mallow plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/White_Marshmallows.jpg/330px-White_Marshmallows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshmallow","wikidata":"Q272198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG/500px-Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG/1280px-Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm